  "title": "Stephane R NDE 5406",
  "date": "15 novembre 2011",
  "content": "I was completely outside time, so I can't say how long the experience lasted. There was a single intense light with no way of fixing its direction or duration. This light was not a blinding light. I myself was a comparable light, partially detached from the other light; I find it difficult to convey this in words. I had a conversation with the light but we did not talk in words. The light emitted a numberless multitude of voices, of incomparable perfection by earthly standards. These voices, all in chorus, sang a single word, which was 'Alleluia', and the length of the chanting of this single word, sung a single time, is quite impossible to express by any measure of earthly time. This one word, 'Alleluia' being sung was at the same time an immense transference of revelations concerning me, the creation, the scriptures, the sense and goal of my own life, and on life and death. When the experience came to an end, I woke up in the resuscitation unit with the conviction that I should not talk about it, but that I also had a duty to do so, that the way in which I should speak about it would come to me in the course of earthly life. At no time in the experience did I see the earth, nor my body, nor any dear ones who had predeceased me.",
